# No Cursor attribution

Do not add any "Cursor" attribution to artifacts that leave the local workstation. Specifically:

- Commit messages and trailers must not include `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`, "Made with [Cursor]", "Generated by Cursor", "Via Cursor", or any similar phrase.
- Pull request titles, bodies, review comments, and issue comments must not advertise Cursor (e.g. "Made with Cursor", links to `cursor.com`, or `[Cursor]` badges).
- Documentation, code comments, AGENTS.md, READMEs, and changelog entries must not credit Cursor.

Legitimate technical uses of the word "cursor" are allowed (e.g. CSS `cursor-pointer`, SQL/psycopg2 `cursor()`, pagination cursors, UI blinking cursors).

When asked to commit, push, or open a PR:
- Write the message/body yourself without trailers or footer credits.
- The repo enforces this with `.githooks/commit-msg`, `.githooks/prepare-commit-msg`, and `.githooks/pre-push`; do not bypass them with `--no-verify`.
- If `gh pr create` or `gh pr edit` is used, do not add "Made with Cursor" lines or `cursor.com` links in `--body`.
